KZ3 patch 2154: invalidate the live-draw state memo after draw-based helper blits.

Adapted from Project Pyrrhus (Killzone 2), patch 6069, same author, MIT.
ld_downsample and ld_scaled_blit bind their own PSO, root signature, heaps and render target.
The next ordinary draw must restore its bindings even when its desired state matches the
memo from before the helper. This correction is unconditional and independent of any
optional recording memo. No new switch or scheduling change.

Host regression: tools/smoke/test_ld_blit_state_memo.py executes the shipped binding
blocks and ordinary memo guards through a fake D3D12 list. It fails on the old code
and detects removal of either invalidation. GPU output is checked separately.

--- a/libs/video/rsx_live_draw.c
+++ b/libs/video/rsx_live_draw.c
@@ -6721,6 +6721,7 @@
     g.list->lpVtbl->SetDescriptorHeaps(g.list, 2, heaps);
     g.list->lpVtbl->SetPipelineState(g.list, pso);
     g.list->lpVtbl->SetGraphicsRootSignature(g.list, g.downsample_rootsig);
+    LD_SM_INVALIDATE();   /* patch 2154: helper draw replaced the ordinary draw bindings */
     const u32 c[5] = {sx, sy, dx, dy, k};
     g.list->lpVtbl->SetGraphicsRoot32BitConstants(g.list, 0, 5, c, 0);
     g.list->lpVtbl->SetGraphicsRootDescriptorTable(g.list, 1, table);
@@ -6859,6 +6860,7 @@
     g.list->lpVtbl->SetDescriptorHeaps(g.list, 2, heaps);
     g.list->lpVtbl->SetPipelineState(g.list, pso);
     g.list->lpVtbl->SetGraphicsRootSignature(g.list, g_sblit_rs);
+    LD_SM_INVALIDATE();   /* patch 2154: helper draw replaced the ordinary draw bindings */
     const float r[4] = { sx / (float)s->w, sy / (float)s->h,
                          (sx + sw) / (float)s->w, (sy + sh) / (float)s->h };
     g.list->lpVtbl->SetGraphicsRoot32BitConstants(g.list, 0, 4, r, 0);
